course: dictionary
lesson: 703
title: Words with a special meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one place, such as a church, a school or a sports field, and they mean something special there. Look at the words around them to find that meaning. «In baptism a person is washed with or dipped in water.» The words washed and water tell you this is about a cleaning ceremony, not a bath at home.
explain: Words can also be used in a picture sense. «The new goalkeeper's first match against the best team was a baptism of fire.» Nobody set the stadium alight. The clue is first match against the best team, so a baptism of fire means a very hard first time at something new.
explain: Ask yourself two questions: what is the topic of this sentence, and what would the word mean if it were a plain fact? If the answer does not fit, the word may have a special or picture meaning. Then check the dictionary.
fact: Baptism is a Christian ceremony in which a person is washed with water or put under water.
fact: At a baptism, the service often takes place for a baby, with family and godparents.
fact: «A baptism of fire» means a very hard first experience of something new.
fact: Some churches baptise only people old enough to choose, often by putting them right under the water. This is called baptism by immersion.
fact: Words with a special meaning often have a clear clue nearby, such as water in the sentence, or a first match in the sentence.
exercise: «In baptism a person is washed with or dipped in water in the name of the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.» What is baptism? | A school exam about water | A kind of birthday cake | *A Christian ceremony in which a person is washed with water | A type of swimming race
exercise: «Many families hold a baptism for a baby, with a white gown, godparents and a party after.» What does baptism mean here? | *A service where a baby is welcomed into the Church with water | A party with no guests | A baby's bath time at home | A school photo day
exercise: «The new goalkeeper's first match against the best team was a baptism of fire.» What does a baptism of fire mean? | A game with no goals | A match played in the rain | *A very hard first experience of something new | A fire drill at school
test: At a baptism, who makes the promise to bring the baby up in the faith? | *The parents and godparents | The children in the school | The baby alone | The whole town by vote
test: «Some churches baptise only people old enough to choose, often by putting them right under the water.» What does «putting them right under the water» describe? | Swimming lessons | Watering plants | Drinking from a river | *Baptism by immersion
exam: In «Churches differ in leaders, baptism, style of worship, use of images and how they read the Bible», what does baptism most likely mean? | *A Christian ceremony with water, which churches may carry out in different ways | A sports prize | A kind of school trip | A type of musical instrument
